    74	  `"３"`); Rust errors on them as unit counts and drops them as market
    75	  quantities.
    76	- **D2:** Python raises `TypeError` when an array or object reaches a dict
    77	  lookup: a unit verb, a PLANT crop (also for missing hands), a PICKUP/PLACE
    78	  item, or a BUY_SEED/BUY_ANIMAL item. Rust treats these as no-ops.
    79	
    80	The vendored kernel bytes are pinned, so nothing was repaired. Seven minimal
    81	repros, one-step games whose first action carries only the divergent field, are
    82	expected-failure fixtures with explicit reasons. Rust asserts the
    83	exact divergence, so a change in either engine fails the test. Full-game
    84	policies exclude D1/D2 inputs by default; with them restored, 8 of 12 games
    85	diverge, all classified D1/D2. The model's grammar emits only ASCII names and
    86	integers, so neither class is reachable from policy actions. An adapter that
    87	accepts external actions would need explicit handling.
    88	
    89	## Verification and limits
    90	
    91	Checks run on this branch are recorded in `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/1.1b/results.md`:
    92	66/66 engine tests, the trim checker, the Python tests (including live
    93	byte-identical regeneration of the committed set), perturbation tests, and
    94	`just prepare`. Codex verification (`verify-1.1b-r1`) approved with edits; the
    95	fixes (confirmed classification, exact null probe, full-state rollback check,
    96	minimal repros, corrected wording) and their checks are recorded in the same
    97	receipt, with the rerun sweep in `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/1.1b/verify-r1/`.
    98	Generated games use weak policies (most random seats go
    99	bankrupt); only the four official episodes are competitive worlds. Kaggle
   100	framework behavior outside the interpreter is not modeled. The 40-game, 303-probe
   101	sweep is a bounded sample, and a pod-scale sweep remains open. Reopen D1/D2 if
   102	the adapter must accept untrusted actions or if the pinned engine changes.
